lines=['# Experiment 3: temporal representation learning','', '## Supervised audit','',f"The B3 checkpoint seed 42 has prediction MSE {a['b3_terms']['prediction']['loss']:.4f}, weighted regularization {a['b3_terms']['regularization']['loss']:.4f}, and unit-weight standardized state MSE {a['b3_terms']['supervision']['loss']:.4f} on the sampled training batch. Corresponding online encoder gradient norms are {a['b3_terms']['prediction']['encoder_grad_norm']:.4f}, {a['b3_terms']['regularization']['encoder_grad_norm']:.4f}, and {a['b3_terms']['supervision']['encoder_grad_norm']:.4f}. These are separate term gradients, not evidence of their combined direction. No target gradients were present. The sampled shapes were video [32,5,3,64,64], state [32,5,4], online slots [32,3,8,32], and head output [32,3,4]. The head is linear, 32 to 4, applied to the mean of eight slots; the target order is ball_x, ball_y, ball_x_vel, ball_y_vel. The training-only mean and standard deviation are stored in the audit JSON. The standardize/inverse round-trip maximum error is {a['normalization_roundtrip_max_error']:.2g}.", '', 'States are saved in sorted key order and explicitly indexed by name. There is one ball with a persistent simulator key, not a list of ball instances. Slot indices are learned queries; nothing assigns them to objects. Previous validation slot audit found B3 slots nearly identical (between-slot MSE 7.46e-5). On validation, mean and concatenated-slot probes gave the following R²:', '', f"- Mean: {fmt(a['slot_probe_validation']['mean']['r2'])}",f"- Concatenated: {fmt(a['slot_probe_validation']['concatenated']['r2'])}",'','Concatenation does not recover a meaningful signal here; this cannot prove pooling never discards object information. B3 is not a pure supervised baseline: competing regularization and prediction terms, a linear head and almost identical slots limit interpretation. No target-order or normalization bug was found.','',f"A 32-example fixed-batch position CNN reduced normalized MSE from {a['single_frame_overfit'][0]['mse']:.4f} to {a['single_frame_overfit'][-1]['mse']:.4f}. A first full-data CNN run trained from scratch converged near constant predictions; its log is retained. The final supervised CNNs use a train-fitted pooled-pixel ridge skip, zero-initialized CNN residual, and Adam at 1e-4. The two-frame CNN concatenates consecutive RGB frames as channels. These are hybrid references, not independently successful CNNs trained from scratch. Eight epochs and validation-selected checkpoints were used. Test R² (x, y, vx, vy):",'',f"- One frame: {fmt(a['supervised_1frame']['test']['all']['r2'])}.",f"- Two frames: {fmt(a['supervised_2frame']['test']['all']['r2'])}.",f"- Existing experiment 2 single-frame pixel ridge: {fmt(b['single_frame']['all']['r2'])}; two-frame pixel ridge: {fmt(b['two_frame']['all']['r2'])}. Those use frames 1–3 rather than only frame 3; comparisons are indicative, not identical test examples.",'','## Design and protocol','', 'All runs use the existing train/validation/test manifests (2400/300/300 independent sequences), first five frames, batch 16, five epochs, AdamW 3e-4, EMA 0.99, seeds 42/43/44. No state or intervention labels enter self-supervised training. The objective is next-context latent MSE + 10×variance-floor penalty + 100×covariance penalty, as in experiment 2 B1. The checkpoint minimizes the same objective on validation batches; training-fit ridge (alpha 100) maps pooled 32-dimensional representations to ball state. Test probes evaluate frame 3; subgroup probes evaluate frame 4 and use the intervention on transition 3→4. For each model, prediction is divided by persistence error in its own EMA latent space. No raw latent MSE is compared across models.','', 'T0 uses the existing framewise eight-query encoder and last frame only, with the existing slot relation/predictor. Unlike experiment 2, all variants here train on one transition per sequence (3→4) rather than all three transitions in the first four frames; the resulting T0 runs are a new matched baseline, not the old checkpoint. T1 and T2 share the same frame CNN and slot encoder. T1 adds two temporal convolutions (the second dilated) per slot with a residual connection; T2 adds a temporal Transformer and learned positions per slot. The final temporal token feeds the same relation and predictor. Target encoding uses the overlapping window shifted by one frame and is stop-gradient. This is one-step prediction between contexts, not a multi-step rollout. Pooling is permutation invariant for the global ball probe; the self-supervised slot loss still assumes that same learned query indices correspond across time. It does not establish object identity.','', 'A fixed-target two-training-sequence overfit check gave initial → final losses: '+ '; '.join(f"{k} {v[0]['loss']:.4g} → {v[-1]['loss']:.4g}" for k,v in tiny.items())+'. Synthetic tests also verify EMA updates, gradients, shapes and dependence on the first context frame.','', '## Held-out results','', '| Model / seed | Position R² x,y | Velocity R² x,y | Effective rank | Std | Prediction / persistence | Params | Train seconds |','|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for k,v in m.items():
 q=v['probe']['r2'];lines.append(f"| {k} | {fmt(q[:2])} | {fmt(q[2:])} | {v['effective_rank']:.2f} | {v['std']:.4f} | {v['subsets']['all']['prediction_to_persistence_ratio']:.3f} | {v['trainable_parameters']} | {v['total_train_seconds']:.1f} |")
lines+=['', 'In this five-epoch comparison, temporal modelling did not meaningfully improve physical-state information: position R² remains near zero and velocity R² is negative across all seeds. T1 and T2 have higher effective rank than T0, but this does not imply a useful state representation. The temporal models also have prediction/persistence ratios above one in all three seeds, so they did not outperform their own persistence baselines.', '', 'The wall time includes validation each epoch and checkpoint I/O, but excludes probe evaluation; hardware is the local Apple MPS device (macOS 26.2 arm64, Python 3.11.15, PyTorch 2.15.0). Parameter counts exclude the frozen EMA copy. Per-seed intervention/no-intervention ratios and state probes are in temporal_metrics.json. Effective rank is the exponential entropy of the pooled covariance spectrum.','', '## Order sensitivity','', 'Each fitted probe is held fixed while its input is reversed, endpoint-preserving shuffled ([2,0,1,3]), or replaced by four copies of the last frame. R² is always scored against the original final-frame state. Reversal changes the final image and therefore confounds temporal direction with position; the endpoint-preserving shuffle and repeat are more specific tests of context dependence, although neither proves a physical motion representation. Normalized changes below are RMS embedding change divided by mean feature standard deviation.','', '| Model / seed | Shuffle / std | Reverse / std | Repeat / std | Repeated-frame velocity R² x,y |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for k,v in m.items():
 q=v['order'];sd=v['std']; lines.append(f"| {k} | {q['shuffle']['representation_rms_change']/sd:.3f} | {q['reverse']['representation_rms_change']/sd:.3f} | {q['repeat']['representation_rms_change']/sd:.3f} | {fmt(q['repeat']['probe_against_original_state']['r2'][2:])} |")
lines += ['', 'The T1 representation changes under an endpoint-preserving shuffle, whereas T2 is nearly invariant to that shuffle in these runs despite responding to repeated frames. Neither has useful velocity probes; the responses do not establish directional motion. Interpret the sensitivity values with the corresponding correct-order probe scores: a change in a weak probe does not establish useful directional motion. These short runs are an exploratory comparison, not evidence of causal understanding or long-horizon rollout capability. The restricted four-frame window, one scalar objective, pooled linear probes, same-query slot loss, single validation objective, and three seeds constrain the conclusion.','', '## Reproduction','', 'From the repository root, with the existing dataset and environment:', '', '```sh', '.venv/bin/python scripts/experiment3_supervised.py', '.venv/bin/python scripts/experiment3_tiny.py', '.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q', '.venv/bin/python scripts/experiment3_temporal.py --epochs 5 --seeds 42 43 44', '.venv/bin/python scripts/plot_experiment3.py', '.venv/bin/python scripts/report_experiment3.py', '```', '', 'The training script refuses to overwrite existing run directories; move or archive experiment3 before reproducing. The interrupted initial T0 attempt is retained and excluded from analysis. Experiment 1 and 2 artifacts and datasets were not modified.']
